+### 5.5a Internal evaluation amendment — SINGLE_OWNER_AI_ASSISTED
+
+Owner decision on 2026-11-22. For internal development review and experimental
+evaluation only, the sole human owner is accountable. Distinct, isolated AI
+roles may implement, author cases, review and freeze. Their model identities,
+access roles, prior exposure, contamination risk and validation limitations
+must be disclosed. No independent human authorship or review is claimed.
+
+Before execution, freeze the exact hidden dataset, corpus, oracle, scorer,
+solver revision, per-arm budgets, order and thresholds. Keep hidden cases and
+gold outside solver access until the preregistered run. Record immutable hashes
+and role/access attestations. Reissue the dataset and freeze on any change.
+The current split is NOT FROZEN. Earlier DEV inputs and results remain
+historical debugging evidence. The 18-case study remains an internal pilot.
+
+This amendment changes the human-role requirement for internal work. The
+remaining freeze controls in §5.6 still apply. The stronger external-evidence
+requirements and Git, security and data controls remain in force. The
+pre-amendment protocol is pinned at
+`0549d27ee561afdf94214cbabe661c2532e08bae`.
